╭ Arch Linux / CachyOS setup ──────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│❯  1 Run automatic setup                                                      │
│   2 Set up data partition                                                    │
│   3 Add kud3n's repository                                                   │
│   4 Install packages                                                         │
│   5 Set up services                                                          │
│   6 Import data                                                              │
│   7 Export data                                                              │
│   8 App status                                                               │
│   9 Inspect a backup                                                         │
│   q Quit                                                                     │
╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯
╭ Details ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│Upgrades the system (pacman -Syuu), adds kud3n's repository, installs every   │
│package, then sets up services. Steps 3 to 5 in one go, with an overall       │
│progress bar and a summary at the end.                                        │
│Changes:    /etc/pacman.conf, installed packages, /etc/pam.d files (backups   │
│kept), Howdy config, systemd services                                         │
│Needs root: yes (kas already runs as root)                                    │
│Automatic:  This is the automatic run (no data partition, no import).         │
│                                                                              │
